-- title:
--   Valuation of a theta value as a weighted cycle pairing
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K_0$, let $\varpi$ be an irreducible element of $R$ with finite residue ring $R/(\varpi)$, and let $K$ be a complete valued extension field of $K_0$ with value group $\Gamma_0$, subject to: every element of $R$ has valuation at most $1$ in $K$ (`hint`); every $a\in K_0$ of valuation at most $1$ lies in the image of $R$ (`hv`); and the powers of $v(\varpi)$ are cofinal towards $0$ in $\Gamma_0$ (`hq`). Let $\varpi_1$ be a pseudo-uniformiser, i.e. an element of $K_0$ whose valuation in $K$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and whose powers bound every valuation from above and below. Let $G$ be a group with a homomorphism $\rho\colon G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ and an action on the vertex set of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $R$, $K_0$ (vertices being homothety classes of full lattices in $K_0^2$, adjacency generated by `VertRel`) which preserves adjacency and satisfies $g\cdot w=\rho(g)\cdot w$ for all $g,w$; assume all vertex stabilisers are finite. Let $\tau$ be a $\mathbb{Z}/2$-valued colouring of vertices, invariant under $G$ and taking distinct values on adjacent vertices, and let $E$ be a finite type equipped with an equivalence $eE$ onto the dart orbits $e$ of $G$ on the tree with $\tau$ of the first vertex of the chosen representative $e.\mathrm{out}$ equal to $0$. Let $g_a,g,g'\in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and let $w_a,w,w'$ lie in the affinoid $\mathrm{affinoid}\ \varpi_1\ 0$, that is, points $z\in K$ with $v(z)\le 1$ and $v(z-a)\ge 1$ for every $a\in K_0$ with $v(a)\le 1$. Assume the colour of $g\cdot$`stdVertex` and the colour of $g'\cdot$`stdVertex` both differ from that of $g_a\cdot$`stdVertex`. Let $P$ be a walk in the tree from $g\cdot$`stdVertex` to $g'\cdot$`stdVertex`, and let $\alpha\in G$. Write $a=\mathrm{pmoebius}(g_a)(w_a)$ (the Möbius action of the class of $g_a$ on $w_a$, read in the affine chart of $\mathbb{P}^1$). Then the valuation of the theta value $\Theta_\rho\bigl(a,\ \rho(\alpha)\!\cdot\! a;\ \mathrm{pmoebius}(g)(w);\ \mathrm{pmoebius}(g')(w')\bigr)$, defined as the multipliable product over $\gamma\in G$ of the cross-ratios $[\,\mathrm{pmoebius}(g')(w'),\ \mathrm{pmoebius}(g)(w);\ \rho(\gamma)a,\ \rho(\gamma)\rho(\alpha)a\,]$, equals $v(\varpi)$ raised to the integer power $-\sum_{e\in E} w(e)\,c_\alpha(e)\,P(e)$, where $w(e)$ is the cardinality of the stabiliser of the dart $(eE\,e).\mathrm{out}$ (as a positive natural number), $c_\alpha(e)$ is the signed dart-orbit count along some path from `stdVertex` to $\alpha\cdot$`stdVertex` (zero if unreachable), and $P(e)$ is the signed dart-orbit count along $P$.
--
--   This is the period law for theta functions on the Drinfeld upper half plane in the form of Manin–Drinfeld: the valuation of a theta quotient built from the orbit of a base point $a$ under $\alpha$ is given by the intersection pairing, weighted by edge-stabiliser widths, between the cycle of $\alpha$ and the cycle of the connecting walk. It is used in the form `v_theta_pmoebius_mul_zpow_sum_stabWidth_mul_pathCycle_mul_walkCycle_eq`, and supplies the statement that the valuation current of the automorphic unit attached to $\alpha$ is the weighted cycle of $\alpha$, an input to the Čerednik–Drinfeld/Mumford uniformisation strand.
